<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38696" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōjecto</span></b> , āre,
			v. freq. a.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to drive forth</i>,
				<i>drive out</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homines in aperta pericula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 5, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to reproach</i>, <i>accuse</i> (ante-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem probris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 3, 6, 38</span></i>
			: ego projector quod tu peccas, Enn. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Rufin. Figur. Sent. p. 222</span></i>
		Ruhnk.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
